WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.990
I am so excited right now

2
00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.570
because we have a huge announcement.

3
00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:05.790
Are you all ready?

4
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.760
Buckle up, and that's a pun intended

5
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.780
because we're taking the Drew Barrymore Show

6
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.670
on the road with the coast to coast

7
00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.953
trip along the iconic Route 66.

8
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.660
From California to New York City.

9
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.200
And we've enlisted this very special couple

10
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.890
to help us make this journey.

11
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:29.223
And here is the story of Karen and Noah Veneklasen.

12
00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:31.880
(applause)

13
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.077
Hi, I'm Karen.

14
00:00:33.077 --> 00:00:33.960
And I'm Noah.

15
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.530
We've got two great kids,

16
00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.580
an amazing golden doodle and five chickens.

17
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.120 line:15%
And we are the founders of Muse and Co. Outdoors,

18
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.480 line:15%
a sprinter van conversion company in Oakland, California.

19
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.470
In March of 2020, we finished a really large project,

20
00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.950
and drew 'em, just absolutely blindsided by the pandemic.

21
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.180
And then all of a sudden, it just hit like a freight train.

22
00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.930
We spent three days going, Oh my gosh,

23
00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.690
we just had to close everything.

24
00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:57.523
What do we do?

25
00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:58.880
We looked around and realized

26
00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:00.870
we actually had a couple of delivery vans

27
00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.510
that just happened to be sprinter vans,

28
00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.580
activated the design team remotely and we designed one.

29
00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.560
Karen and I took the thing and headed up the post

30
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.245
with the kids.

31
00:01:09.245 --> 00:01:10.280
People would come up to us,

32
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.870
they were flocking into the van

33
00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:15.020
and we realized how much interest there was in these.

34
00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.940
And it just absolutely built a love for travel

35
00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.975
that both in recreation and business.

36
00:01:19.975 --> 00:01:22.246
I just started to realize how big the world is

37
00:01:22.246 --> 00:01:23.910
and developed the absolute love for it.

38
00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:25.370
Traveling to the next state

39
00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.120
can be an eye-opening adventure.

40
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.150
You're seeing something new that you've never seen before.

41
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.860
And that to me is really the power of the travel experience.

42
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.860
We are so unbelievably excited to be

43
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.230
heading out on the road for you.

44
00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.411
And can't wait to see you in a few days.

45
00:01:38.411 --> 00:01:39.340
(audience applause and cheering)

46
00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.760
Here they are, it's Karen and Noah,

47
00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.808
They're joining us before they hit the road.

48
00:01:45.808 --> 00:01:46.641
Hi, guys!

49
00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.230
Hi Drew, nice to meet you.

50
00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:56.000
Oh, thank you guys so much for doing this with us.

51
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.130
I am just so glad that you guys are representing that

52
00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:03.820
lifestyle and talking about the whimsy and the wonder

53
00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:08.073 line:15%
of how extraordinary life in this sprinter van can be.

54
00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.460
It is, it's limitless, Drew you know,

55
00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.200
it's so amazing just to pull in anywhere you want.

56
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.280
You're not even bound by campgrounds,

57
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.350
you just kind of fall in wherever you want.

58
00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.550
It's amazing.

59
00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:23.440
Where are you guys now and when do you leave?

60
00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.470
Yeah, so greetings from Oakland, California.

61
00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:30.263
That's where we are from, that's where the company is.

62
00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.130 line:15%
We're leaving after this, Drew,

63
00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.150 line:15%
we are getting on the road

64
00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.500 line:15%
as soon as we hang up with you.

65
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.980 line:15%
We are quite literally heading off across the country.

66
00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.790
We will see you in nine days.

67
00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.610
I'm excited you're about to hit the road.

68
00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:44.940
Karen, who will you be meeting along the way?

69
00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:48.153
We are going to be doing a Barrymore tour,

70
00:02:49.336 --> 00:02:51.860
it's a surprise location, I'm not gonna give it away

71
00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:56.860
but I will say, it might be just a tad scary

72
00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.543
but it might also be amazing.

73
00:02:59.905 --> 00:03:02.480
I'm intrigue.

74
00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.693
I am too, believe me.

75
00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.863
We're gonna be meeting some really inspiring Drew gooder.

76
00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.860
And then of course, we're gonna be checking in

77
00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.950
with a small business owner

78
00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.360
and celebrating the amazing job that they've done

79
00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.480
keeping themselves and their employees afloat

80
00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.050
during this whole pandemic, and we're gonna do more.

81
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.850
We'll share it all with you when we get there.

82
00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:24.500
Well, over the next nine days, we're gonna be with you,

83
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:27.900
checking in as you make your way here to the show

84
00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.548
in New York.

85
00:03:29.548 --> 00:03:31.000
(applause)
That's right.

86
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:35.433
That's the end destination, I'll be here with open arms.

87
00:03:36.587 --> 00:03:39.550
If you spot the Drew Van in your town,

88
00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.240
be sure to take a photo

89
00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:45.333
and send it to the show or post it on social media.

90
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.720
You just might see your picture on the air.

91
00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:50.960
That's right, 'cause we're gonna show

92
00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.120
some of these pictures.

93
00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.960
I'm gonna feature some on my social media,

94
00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.430
by the way, did you guys get some of the

95
00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.630
Drew's News stickers too, do you have those?

96
00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:00.670
Yeah, we did.

97
00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.963
And they're already getting stuck.

98
00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:04.990
Perfect

99
00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:06.340
All over for people to find.

100
00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.990
I love seeing stickers and I feel like it's a lost art.

101
00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.950
So we printed a bunch of Drew's News stickers.

102
00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.990
So if you see those around, tag us too.

103
00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:16.890
All right, Karen and Noah, Veneklasen, safe travels

104
00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:20.160
with you on the road, we will be here waiting

105
00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.240
but checking in with you all along the way.

106
00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:27.180
And seriously, if you spot that Drew Van, let us know.

107
00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.605
Thank you Drew, we're so excited to get there.

108
00:04:30.605 --> 00:04:32.106
Thank you Noah and Karen.

109
00:04:32.106 --> 00:04:34.939
(uplifting music)

